RefuseRefuse currently runs as a browser-first app with a FastAPI backend and a Vite frontend.

Quick start

- `cp .env.compose.example .env` (first time only)
- `npm run start` to start backend + frontend + proxy in detached mode
- Open `http://localhost:5173`

Compose workflow

- `npm run dev` to run app services in the foreground
- `npm run logs` to stream app service logs
- `npm run status` to inspect compose service status
- `npm run stop` to stop compose services

Analytics profile (optional)

- `npm run analytics:up` to start Postgres + Airflow + dbt helper container
- `npm run analytics:logs` to stream analytics service logs
- `npm run analytics:dbt:shell` to run dbt commands interactively
- `npm run analytics:down` to stop analytics profile services
- Starter DAG: `analytics/airflow/dags/refuserefuse_starter_dag.py` (appears as `refuserefuse_starter` in Airflow UI)
- Airflow UI: `http://localhost:8080` (defaults from `.env`: `admin` / `admin`)

Proxy/API behavior

- Browser traffic goes to nginx on `http://localhost:5173`.
- Frontend calls API using relative `/api` paths.
- Nginx rewrites `/api/*` to backend routes on the internal compose network.

For full setup, run commands, and architecture notes, use `ARCHITECTURE.md` as the source of truth.

Current local workflow

- `npm run start` starts app services via Docker Compose
- `npm run stop` stops app services
- `npm run status` shows whether compose services are running

Project layout

- `backend/` contains the FastAPI API and local SQLite data
- `frontend/` contains the Vite browser app
- `mobile/` contains the Expo mobile app shell

Mobile plan

The earlier Expo scaffold was intentionally removed from the repo root so the active app stayed unambiguous. Mobile now lives in its own dedicated `mobile/` directory instead of sharing the root with the browser app.

Mobile quick start

- `cd mobile && npm install`
- `npm run mobile:start` from the repo root, or `npm start` inside `mobile/`
- Set `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` if you are running on a device instead of a simulator

Social auth quick setup

- Copy and customize env templates:
	- `backend/.env.example`
	- `frontend/.env.example`
	- `mobile/.env.example`
- Backend must be started with `GOOGLE_CLIENT_IDS` and `APPLE_AUDIENCES` configured.
- Frontend uses Google and Apple JS SDKs and exchanges provider ID tokens with backend OAuth endpoints.
- Mobile uses Expo Google/Apple sign-in and exchanges provider ID tokens with backend OAuth endpoints.
